 ## 1. Lexicon
 
 | Term | Meaning |
 |---|---|
-| MMF | Minimum Marketable Feature. A small, self-contained feature that can be developed quickly and that gives the user significant value (Agile Alliance). Not an MVP. |
+| MMF | Minimum Marketable Feature: a small, self-contained feature that can be developed quickly and that delivers significant value to the user (Agile Alliance glossary). Not an MVP. Each MMF states a benefit hypothesis (`D-479` item 1). |
 | Enabler | Work that makes MMFs possible or releasable, with no direct user value of its own (SAFe term). |
-| IP iteration | Innovation and Planning iteration. A buffer iteration with no feature work (SAFe 6.0). |
-| `TASKS-S1`..`S4` | The four sprints in the historical `docs/TASKS.md`. |
-| `PRD-S0`..`S6` | The sprint rows in `docs/Modular_PRD.md` §8.1. Different content from `TASKS-S*`. |
